# marker-dialect-closure.rq (PROJ-622)
# Marker: GRAPHLAW_DIALECT_CLOSURE.
# Inputs: OBSERVATION graph UNION hooks/dialect-registry.ttl (the marker
# store loads the registry TTL alongside the obs + evidence graphs — vocab
# gap (e) resolved: hook_standing and hook_receipt observations now carry
# ex:dialect, whose value is the dreg: DialectEntry IRI of the dialect the
# graphlaw hooks engine actually executed — dreg:delta for the workday
# packs, whose hooks are all kind "delta").
# Closure direction — deliberately governance-shaped: every dialect
# OBSERVED in hook evidence must be REGISTERED (no unregistered dialect
# ever executes). The inverse claim ("every registered dialect was
# exercised") is NOT made: the registry deliberately registers dialects
# (n3, shex, owl-rl, ...) that the workday broker does not route, and a
# marker may only claim what is emitted.
# Output: single row ?value = COUNT(DISTINCT observed dialects that are not
# a registered dreg:DialectEntry). Expectation: 0.
# Determinism: aggregate + NOT EXISTS over a fixed graph.
PREFIX obs:  <https://ggen.io/ontology/bench-obs#>
PREFIX ex:   <http://example.org/rwai#>
PREFIX dreg: <http://seanchatmangpt.github.io/praxis/dreg#>

SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?dialect) AS ?value)
WHERE {
  ?o obs:obsKind ?kind ;
     ex:dialect ?dialect .
  FILTER(?kind IN ("hook_standing", "hook_receipt"))
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?dialect a dreg:DialectEntry . }
}
